WEBVTT

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.070
That's a nice windmill!

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:13.200
Well, Helshper's capital is also known as
the City of Windmills.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.990
Those windmills pump up water,
and deliver it to the rest of the city.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.680
So it's got aqueducts?

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.410
The castle sticks out, though…

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:29.420
Talk about East meeting West.
Where and when is it supposed to be from?

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.970
East meeting West? What an odd-sounding phrase.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:41.390
Um, I guess it's an expression
for when two differing cultures mix together?

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:45.150
And you call that East meeting West? I see.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.490
Hearing the reasoning, it fits perfectly.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:50.090
He accepted that quick.

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:54.190
Ah, but I was supposed to be
taking you to Sakaiya.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:55.850
It's this way.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.110
Still,

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:02.720
you're even acquainted with Sakaiya's own Caerick?

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:04.100
I'm surprised.

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:08.820
Oh, I don't know him.
I was just asked to bring him a letter.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.790
Cayna, do you know much of Sakaiya?

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:14.400
No, nothing at all.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:18.210
I've never met anyone who didn't know about it.

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:20.810
Is it really that famous of a store?

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:25.390
It's not just famous, it's
the largest mercantile house on the continent.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:30.120
From a grain of wheat to a magic item,
you can get anything you want there.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:34.520
You can even hire soldiers.
It's said there's nothing they don't have.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:37.800
So it's like a big general trading company?

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:42.310
We also do a lot of business with them.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.420
I should have known!

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:49.590
Okay, I'm on it!

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:51.330
This is Sakaiya.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.890
This is quite an impressive building!

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:54.750
But…

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:56.710
That tile roof…

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:59.920
East meeting West never looked more chaotic!

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:01.680
Oh, if it isn't Elineh!

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.890
You've had quite the trip.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.280
My, if it isn't the young master.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.600
I'm in your hands yet again.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:11.690
Is the old master in?

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:15.000
We have a letter from Felskeilo.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:16.780
A letter, you say?

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.520
May I read it over?

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:20.420
Certainly.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.390
Here it is.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:22.820
Thank you.

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:29.430
Pl…

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.510
Please wait just a moment!

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:08.980
[Grandson, Granddaughter,
Great-Grandson, and Fort]

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:13.480
[Sakai]

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:16.670
It has been far too long, Elineh.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.690
I'm glad to see you, as well, Caerick.

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:24.690
I hear you've been wheeling and dealing
your way into as much money as ever.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.100
Much obliged.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:30.310
Oh, hel… lo?

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:34.390
Caerick's bowing to someone other than royalty?!

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.410
It is very nice to meet you,

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:38.890
Grandmother.

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:40.290
Grandmother?!

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:46.000
Yes. I am your daughter
Mai-Mai's son, Caerick Sakai.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:48.020
Mai-Mai's son?

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:51.720
My mother has told me great things about you.

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:55.710
To think I would get to meet
the wielder of treasures herself…

00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:58.100
I am truly honored.

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:04.690
Grandmother, you appear to be
quite tired from your journey here!

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:07.150
Before you use a squalid inn in town,

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:10.480
I shall prepare you a splendid, high-class room,

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:12.420
so why don't you stay here?

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:13.080
[Sakai]
so why don't you stay here?

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:17.000
Oh, don't worry about me. I'm not tired.

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:20.500
I've just had my eyes opened
to a shocking truth, is all.

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:23.210
Mai-Mai won't be getting off easy.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:30.920
Grandmother?

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:33.780
Oh, and about those "squalid" inns…

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:40.300
I find their food and my time with the people
who stay at them to be quite valuable,

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:44.310
so they would relax me more than
your splendid, high-class rooms,

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:46.810
so please… Don't. Mind. Me.

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:52.070
Have I… said something to o-offend you?

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:53.310
No! Nothing at all!

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:57.680
Anyway, my business here is done, so do excuse me.

00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:01.320
Ah, C-Cayna! Excuse me, Caerick.

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:02.790
[Sakai]

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:04.600
[Sakai]
Please, wait for me, Cayna!

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:05.420
[Sakai]

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:07.470
We're back!

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.300
Yup, back.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:12.670
Hey, welcome back, Mr. Elineh, Missy.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:14.200
Yo, welcome!

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:18.510
These are Helshper knights.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:22.900
They had some questions about
the bandits we met at the eastern border.

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:24.800
That makes sense.

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:27.420
We just finished explainin' what happened.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:31.010
We're giving them the staff the bandit had.

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:32.010
That okay?

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:34.200
Indeed. No problem at all.

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:35.290
In that case…

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.290
Can we consider our business concluded?

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:40.120
Yes, thank you.

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:42.310
You two, please wait outside.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:43.220
Yes, ma'am.

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:52.220
What? Why?

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:55.800
It seems your mood has been rather spoiled.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:58.540
Allow me to apologize for my little brother.

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:00.200
I am truly sorry,

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:01.520
Grandmother.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:05.460
Grandmother?!

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:08.120
Y-You wouldn't happen to be…

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:12.400
I am Caerick's older twin sister, Caerina Sakai.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:17.190
Yeah, you do look a lot like that creep.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:23.030
Calling him "that creep"…
My brother must have been quite rude to you.

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:27.290
That said, I'm surprised
how well-informed you are. We only just met him.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:32.590
We have the ability to converse
even without being in one another's presence.

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:35.910
Extra Skill: Telepathy, huh?

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:41.310
Well guessed, Grandmother! Again,
I am truly sorry about what my brother did.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:44.270
You don't have to apologize so much for it.

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:47.100
I was also acting a bit childish.

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:52.700
I'm glad you'd say that.
Our mother has told us much about you.

00:07:53.180 --> 00:07:55.520
My brother was quite terrified.

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:58.040
And what, exactly, did she tell you?

00:07:58.390 --> 00:08:04.110
When angry, you fiendishly grind even your
relatives into a fine paste, without any mercy.

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:05.300
No, I don't!

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:10.710
Missy, I don't think you should go
grinding your relatives into paste.

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:13.550
H-Have you really done something so awful?!

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:15.220
No, never!

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:18.620
Do you really see me
as some indiscriminate murderer?!

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:19.740
More an ice flower.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:25.290
N-No, I mean that bandit
sure turned into a pretty ice sculpture!

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:28.030
It was a compliment!

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:29.970
In what way is that a compliment?!

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:31.980
It really was pretty!

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:33.480
It was indeed pretty!

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:35.010
Yup, pretty!

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:38.200
Why are you all on the same page?!

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:44.520
That does it! Nobody can blame me
for getting mad now!

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:48.800
C-Cayna…

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:53.120
W-Wait, Missy! Calm down!
Just put that down on the floor!

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:56.180
W-When did you get a huge snowball?!

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:58.800
Enough talk! Fire!

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:08.770
Why'd she hit me, too?

00:09:08.990 --> 00:09:10.480
S-So pretty…

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:25.500
I just wanted to orchestrate a touching
first meeting between Mother and my children…

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:29.130
And then Caerina used Telepathy to tell you,

00:09:29.390 --> 00:09:36.200
"Caerick angered Grandmother,
and it almost cost lives. What should we do?"

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:38.320
Let me think…

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:45.300
I want to stand up for them, but if I did,
Our Mother's ire would be redirected at me.

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:54.690
While you did bring this on yourself
by attempting to surprise Our Mother,

00:09:55.160 --> 00:10:01.120
well, when she returns, I shall apologize
alongside you. Do cheer up.

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:04.380
Okay. Thank you, Skargo.

00:10:04.810 --> 00:10:06.790
She's being unusually earnest.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:10.320
I guess even Mai-Mai has a lovable side.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:14.090
I guess even Skargo had a nice side.

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:18.880
That was all your fault, Caerick.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:21.670
I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry…

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:24.810
I have no ball in this court.

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:26.530
I have balls!

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:33.390
All the requests are from merchants…

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:37.240
Most of 'em want bandits dealt with, huh?

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.090
Excuse me.

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:42.500
What's up, girlie?

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:47.120
Wait, you're an adventurer, too? Pretty tiny one.

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:50.260
So's everyone else, from your perspective.

00:10:51.820 --> 00:10:54.890
Haven't seen you around.
You just become an adventurer?

00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:57.830
No, I came from Felskeilo.

00:10:58.190 --> 00:10:59.880
So, what's going on?

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:04.810
I heard there was a place with a castle on a lake.

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:06.880
Do you know where it might be?

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:08.070
Oh, that?

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:09.890
That's Crescent-Moon Castle.

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:11.440
This is it.

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:16.510
It's deep in bandit lands,
so nobody can get close.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:19.800
Why's it called Crescent-Moon Castle?

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:24.420
Because the whole castle glows
on crescent-moon nights.

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:25.550
Wow!

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:28.620
Rumors say it's an ancient treasury,

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:34.310
but ask some old fogeys and they're all terrified,
calling it a "Guardian's Manse."

00:11:34.430 --> 00:11:37.090
A Guardian's Manse? That sounds promising!

00:11:37.850 --> 00:11:40.550
Thank you very much! You were a big help!

00:11:40.910 --> 00:11:42.290
Don't sweat it.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:45.210
You could get this info anywhere.

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:48.000
Um, is something wrong?

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:49.500
Oh, no, I…

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:52.630
Don't sweat it.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:57.120
He's just a lecher with a habit
of practically staring holes in girls' faces.

00:11:58.440 --> 00:11:59.780
Oh, is that what it was?

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:01.610
I'll be off, then.

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:05.330
Anyone would be suspicious, bud.

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:09.150
I just felt like I'd seen her somewhere…

00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:11.500
Really, that old pickup line?

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:14.820
She's an elf! They're all hot!

00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:18.420
I wasn't hitting on her!
I swear, I've seen her somewhere.

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:21.970
Says the guy who chats up every elf he sees!

00:12:22.790 --> 00:12:24.180
You dropped character.

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:25.300
Whoops!

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:29.590
Oopsie-daisy! I'm a girl, I'm a girl, I'm a girl…

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:31.590
[I'm a girl…]
Where have I seen her before?

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:36.480
So, where should I go from here?
I do want some more detailed info…

00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:42.040
The bandit cleanup requests all came
from merchants, so maybe Caerick would know more?

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:45.720
Are you certain? He was terrified.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:50.060
I already said I was being childish.

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:53.680
Well, nothing for it but to see
if we can go make up.

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:01.920
Well…

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:04.420
Anyway, uh…

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:06.240
Sorry.

00:13:06.710 --> 00:13:08.910
No, don't grind me into paste!

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:14.520
Paste again? Mai-Mai told you about that, right?

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:15.670
It was Mai-Mai?

00:13:16.090 --> 00:13:16.860
Yes?

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:20.600
What shall I do with my idiot daughter?

00:13:20.990 --> 00:13:22.710
Oh, right, Caerick!

00:13:22.830 --> 00:13:23.590
Y-Yes?

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:27.950
Could you use Telepathy to send Mai-Mai a message?

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:32.100
Y-Y-Y-Yes! What m-m-message should I send?

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:36.450
"Given iron maiden, guillotine, crucifixion,

00:13:36.610 --> 00:13:38.620
live burial, burning alive,

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:41.740
quartering, crushing weights, and pear of anguish,

00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:44.460
which would you choose?", if you'd be so kind.

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:47.730
O-Okay. It's on its way.

00:13:51.090 --> 00:13:55.500
I have made embarrassing remarks
unbefitting of a leader of merchants.

00:13:55.820 --> 00:13:58.010
I ask your forgiveness, Grandmother.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:01.520
It's fine, no need to apologize.

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:04.230
I'm sure you were looking out for me.

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:06.210
Plus I was a bit childish.

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:07.490
Anyway!

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:08.150
Yes?

00:14:08.770 --> 00:14:12.830
I want to ask you about
the Crescent-Moon Castle in this country.

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:14.730
What about it?

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:17.810
It seems an awful lot
like a Guardian Tower, right?

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:19.100
What did you say?!

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:24.920
Do you mean the thirteen god-granted pillars
supporting this world?!

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:30.550
The mysterious towers that house supreme treasures
but that only the chosen may enter?!

00:14:30.710 --> 00:14:33.610
Yeah. Though that's a bit exaggerated…

00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:39.210
Anyway, I wanted to go in and wake up its guardian
before it breaks down. Shore it up, y'know?

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:42.590
I was thinking I'd go tomorrow.

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:47.500
I'm sorry to tell you, Grandmother,
but it's currently in bandit territory…

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:49.910
Oh, that'll work itself out.

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:57.690
It's not my main goal, but if they get in my way,
I might just take those bandits out.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:14:58.910
Catch my drift?

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:00.320
Grandmother…

00:15:01.110 --> 00:15:05.100
With the bandits gone,
we could reopen the main road…

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:11.610
But even if I get rid of the bandits,
keep my part in it under wraps.

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:12.820
May I ask why?

00:15:13.400 --> 00:15:17.900
Think. The knights are
having trouble with those bandits.

00:15:18.280 --> 00:15:20.450
If word got out a little girl did 'em in…

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:24.000
If that happened, I'd hole up again.

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:26.840
I don't want to be in the spotlight.

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:30.800
Grandmother, just one thing.

00:15:32.630 --> 00:15:38.100
The knights have a garrison
shutting down traffic to the lake.

00:15:38.420 --> 00:15:40.230
But we can get around that, right?

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:41.680
Of course.

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:45.440
My sister was sent there
on a mission a few days ago.

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:48.020
We'll pull some strings to get you through.

00:15:48.390 --> 00:15:53.520
My, is it acceptable for Sakaiya to aid
a single adventurer, for all the world to see?

00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:55.340
It's no problem whatsoever.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:16:03.310
That adventurer will be on an important
resupply mission to that very garrison.

00:16:05.350 --> 00:16:07.710
I see Sakaiya has a dark side.

00:16:08.140 --> 00:16:11.700
Oh, no, we can't hold a candle
to you, Grandmother.

00:16:17.710 --> 00:16:22.330
Thank goodness Great-Grandmother
didn't grind Father up…

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:29.210
Thank you.

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:32.480
Y-You're welcome! Least I could do.

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:42.090
Anyway, I got hired by Caerick
to deliver supplies to a garrison,

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:44.390
so I'll be out for a couple days.

00:16:44.490 --> 00:16:49.990
Is that so? I'm relieved
that you made amends with Caerick.

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:56.890
I'm sorry I caused you so much trouble, Elineh.

00:16:57.220 --> 00:17:00.820
I doubt anything could
cause you any trouble, Missy,

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:02.860
but it never hurts to be careful.

00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:07.800
We'll be needing your skills
on the way back to Felskeilo,

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:09.750
so please do take care.

00:17:09.990 --> 00:17:14.070
I will. Thanks, Elineh, Arbiter.

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:22.130
Stop for a bit.

00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:26.750
Nobody's looking, right?

00:17:27.070 --> 00:17:27.850
Okay.

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:30.430
Summon Magic: Veldocancer.

00:17:46.470 --> 00:17:51.590
Alright, Veld, you're carrying us
to the knights' garrison, okay?

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:08.610
Yes, Grandmother,
Caerick contacted me via Telepathy

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:14.320
and said that you would bring us supplies
and that we were to let you proceed to the lake.

00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:17.450
But that was just this morning!

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:22.900
The trip should take three days
by horse, so how are you already here?!

00:18:23.090 --> 00:18:27.220
I though you'd want the resupply,
so I rushed over,

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:29.230
but now you're blaming me?

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:33.610
N-No, I'm not blaming you, I'm just confused.

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:39.110
Excuse me, Captain, is this adventurer
an acquaintance of yours?

00:18:39.610 --> 00:18:40.860
She is my grandmother.

00:18:41.790 --> 00:18:44.680
Still, treat her as you would any guest.

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:46.000
Y-Yes, ma'am.

00:18:46.170 --> 00:18:47.130
Also…

00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:50.610
R-Reporting!

00:18:51.350 --> 00:18:52.420
It's a raid!

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:53.380
What?!

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:54.340
Who are they?

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:57.000
The enemy is believed to be rock golems!

00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:58.270
Nine of them!

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:00.370
Nine rock golems?

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:02.920
Have all hands prepare to intercept.

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:03.700
On it!

00:19:04.390 --> 00:19:07.300
Grandmother, you stay put here.

00:19:07.810 --> 00:19:08.660
Is that clear?

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:11.490
Hm? Maybe I won't.

00:19:11.860 --> 00:19:13.660
It's on you if you get hurt.

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:14.630
Let's go.

00:19:14.830 --> 00:19:15.280
Okay!

00:19:18.580 --> 00:19:20.020
You're not helping?

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:23.200
Should I, though?

00:19:23.670 --> 00:19:28.520
What should I do?
I really don't want to stand out…

00:19:39.290 --> 00:19:40.780
They are rock golems…

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:43.090
Archers, fire at will!

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:43.940
Yes, ma'am!

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:50.940
Damn, that did nothing!

00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:53.420
It's as I feared.

00:19:53.890 --> 00:19:58.710
Only impact weapons like hammers
and maces can damage them.

00:19:59.020 --> 00:19:59.840
But…

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:04.410
We only have 20 knights,
and they're all swordsmen.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:07.100
Captain, let's go and hit them!

00:20:07.240 --> 00:20:11.610
Yeah! We can't let them go any further!

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:12.650
Captain!

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:19.200
I don't think we can beat rock golems,
but we're out of time.

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:23.020
At this rate, the garrison will be destroyed.

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:27.910
Then there'd be nobody left
to protect the capital from bandits and monsters.

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:31.300
We have to do everything in our power.

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:35.120
We're going out there! Don't let them get past us!

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:35.980
Yes, ma'am!

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:37.340
Swords at the ready!

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:43.210
- My sword for the captain!
- For Helshper!

00:20:43.480 --> 00:20:45.100
- Their advance stops here!
- To victory!

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:47.820
- Strike 'em hard and fast!
- We're with you!

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:54.200
Keep your guards up!

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:56.490
Charge!

00:21:05.190 --> 00:21:06.500
Not even a scratch?

00:21:18.280 --> 00:21:19.350
Hang in there!

00:21:19.570 --> 00:21:20.880
Get him to the garrison!

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:24.920
Weapon Skill:

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:30.000
Fire Blade!

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:35.700
Nice one, Captain!

00:21:35.840 --> 00:21:38.300
Did you see that, you damn rock toys?!

00:21:40.310 --> 00:21:41.100
Captain…

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:42.210
I'm fine.

00:21:42.660 --> 00:21:44.070
But it is, too…

00:21:46.110 --> 00:21:47.060
No way!

00:21:47.380 --> 00:21:49.310
If even that wasn't enough,

00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:51.970
retreat is the only option left.

00:21:56.190 --> 00:21:59.030
Very nicely done! Was that self-taught?

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:02.410
It takes talent to do that much
with self-taught skills.

00:22:02.740 --> 00:22:03.750
Grandmother?

00:22:07.210 --> 00:22:09.150
Leave the rest to me.
